      "message": "Not sure which change needs this comment, so copying to both.\n\n@Jeff this also affected NDR tests (dpdk plugin and E810CQ NIC) in a way that looks very similar to the issue I fixed in https://gerrit.fd.io/r/c/vpp/+/45953\nBasically, without any interrupt/timeout there was no mechanism to flush the final 1-3 packets after a test ended. The difference is that in iavf it affected all directions/queues equally, in dpdk only one direction for some reason. I suspect the same fix (one interrupt that \"does nothing\" but indirectly flushes trailing packets) will work, assuming the action happens at low enough frequency (microseconds?) to not have a big effect during peak traffic.",
